2026-11-03T15:17:39.8481310Z   "box_background_custody_selected_here": false,
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8483240Z   "box_background_custody_scope": "Existing daemon background registry retains actual Child, readers, controller and file outcomes; ordinary/timed admission, bounded stop and no stale signaling, pre-spawn refusal and entered uncertainty, exact Host/ForeverBox/Runner custody and actual terminal-watch settlement. Canonical terminal final bytes are consumed without test rewriting. Private operation-fault producer remains separately identified from the shipping daemon. Normal active streamed shutdown, arbitrary descendant trees, terminal authenticity, durable restart, real services/devices, packages and full OCRM acceptance remain open.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8488150Z   "box_shell_capture_scope": "Actual daemon foreground capture distinguishes pre-spawn known refusal from entered read/wait/worker uncertainty for ordinary Shell and MiniSwe. Owned children and incomplete captures remain in the same registry under nonreusable invocation identities through bounded observed cleanup; exhaustion refuses before spawn and streamed stop/handoff preserves exact invocation custody. Exceptional stream returns/unwinds retain the real Child and started readers; completed recovery is observed after bounded cleanup or at ordinary/stream admission without requiring shutdown, while inherited-pipe custody remains pending until actual EOF; actual Throw/Close reaches Host, ForeverBox, Runner sticky custody, no replay and checkpoint refusal. Private cfg(test) operation faults are bound to a separately identified library test artifact; normal shipping daemon controls remain independent. Descendant-process closure, hostile ownership changes, raw HTML provenance, power loss, platform packages and real services remain unaccepted.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8488340Z   "box_response_contract": "BXR-v1.3",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8490450Z   "box_response_scope": "Actual existing manager/accessor identity, protobuf/HTTP/Connect completion, typed post-write uncertainty, ForeverBox Shell/Read/Write/ComputerUse projection and actual MCP spill bridge. Real owned daemon Shell/binary Write/Read uses the same production accessor and nonzero identities. Controlled peers do not prove external services, real monitor devices, cancellation, raw HTML capture, persistence, packages or all-platform compatibility. Existing downstream effect-custody tests are reused inside codex-model-regressions.",
