2026-11-03T15:17:39.8569000Z   "fresh_bearer_admission_scope": "Actual existing pairing owner refuses a fresh proof when the approved role or whole canonical live grant is no longer current, preserves fixed decisive-storage errors and exact durable state, and admits repaired valid state after reopen. Retained proof checks keep their existing issuer and late-admission semantics. Actual HTTP config.set through the App Settings helper and shipping source bindings are separately required in the App receipt; these owner controls do not establish full App construction, remote handshake, last-use writes, issuer-generation or physical-device acceptance.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8570450Z   "media_settlement_support_scope": "MSU-v1 support only: actual Tool construction-error classification and the independently bounded media COMMIT adapter/consumer proof, composed with all retained channel/admission/raw-COMMIT controls. Real file-backed media DB faults and local cleanup states are required by the separate native-media receipt; eight private App/Session/Runner cases and ordinary shipping feature-off compilation are required by the separate Linux App receipt. No runtime or full acceptance is inferred from source-oracle positives.",
