2026-11-03T15:17:39.8574280Z   "memory_synthesis_identity_scope": "Per-snapshot MemorySynthesis uses one admitted model/credential identity across proposal, verification and retries. Native and Codex controls reach the production factory, actual HTTP assembly, Session apply gate and FileMemoryStore with owned credentials. Same-context token rotation is accepted; account/workspace drift and cancellation preserve memory/temporal bytes. Stale starts a new snapshot admission. Detached-worker drain, atomic cancellation/commit, original evidence account binding, durable synthesis recovery and real providers remain unaccepted.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8578020Z   "send_message_fidelity_scope": "SGF-v1 preserves actual completed SendMessage producer wire through existing canonical field 2 independently of live observation, using a fresh invocation recorder and checked receipt/callback/drain custody. Actual Session success-only decoding retains full-envelope and effective oneof semantics through backfill/reopen. Controlled actual App SQL sends compare message identity, normalized arguments, timestamps, live/canonical bytes and Journal projection; original typed failure, completion revocation and two fresh owner reads retain no replay or marker authority. Real providers/channels, external delivery ACK, lost SQL identity reconstruction, original interrupted-turn restart, rich variants and packaged-platform acceptance remain open.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8579020Z   "codex_workspace_binding_scope": "Actual private credential loading, per-turn source/workspace continuity, same-workspace rotation, recreated retry/checkpoint refusal, one-401 refresh before persistence and bound/fresh Memory consumers through real HTTP with owned redirected destinations. Real service, external-writer settlement and process-restart acceptance remain open.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8580890Z   "generated_history_scope": "Actual generated Runner retains ordered known successful tool observations and the accepted user through the existing canonical root/Journal transaction after provider failure or cancellation. Owned fresh processes observe history without provider/tool replay or completion/marker authority. Real provider-store refusal retains unaccepted effect custody; unknown/no-effect/root-drift controls, original typed error preservation, prior-completion invalidation and ordinary success remain required. Controlled Responses do not prove real provider compatibility, unknown/pending history, complete typed replay/UI, original-turn restart or packaged-platform acceptance.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8582720Z   "canonical_root_admission_scope": "Actual checked optional canonical snapshots bind Host composition, Runner projection, preflight, staging and guarded publication. Required process controls distinguish absent/present-empty and legacy-root identities, strict read/retirement refusals, same-sink successor drift, early-error permanent completion revocation, and post-durable Journal failure with fresh-owner recovery. Controlled Responses are not real provider compatibility. No lock spans provider execution; MCP catalog preparation precedes admission; recursive graph validation, prior-root wire provenance, original-turn restart, complete typed replay and package acceptance remain open.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8584340Z   "plugin_uninstall_recovery_scope": "Durable pre-dispatch tickets and exact settlements in the existing MCP/Skills owner, pending and confirmed refusal in actual Session/prompt consumers, strict image/marker recovery, cache-before-release barriers, and same-root Host handoff. Owned producer process exits and fresh consumer processes use controlled backend I/O. Pending outcomes are never replayed or cleared by ordinary sync. Account/backend incarnation, remote receipt/quiescence reconciliation, real ecosystem, hardware power-loss and packaged-platform acceptance remain open.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8585870Z   "checkpoint_publication_scope": "Actual provider checkpoint writer: private owned staging, exact payload preservation, no-clobber final publication, directory-entry barriers including retry after a failed creation barrier, and retained visible payload after a controlled final barrier failure. Actual shell adapter retains a completed file effect as uncheckpointed after real store refusal and explicit repair. No original-turn restart eligibility, claim or execution, hardware power-loss or packaged-platform acceptance.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8587750Z   "session_namespace_scope": "SNI-v1 runs the complete existing path, Agent lifecycle and Agent Session targets. Real Session/Human stores cover reserved Agent path refusal before locks, markers and caches; whole-batch lifecycle and Gateway preflight before all hooks; distinct typed Agent/Human cache owners in both opening orders; Agent close/retire/delete, unchanged Human bytes and reopen; and retained valid deletion/admission controls. Colon-bearing filesystem controls run on Unix. This is not every filesystem alias, external parent replacement, Windows or packaged acceptance, Human attachment admission, membership revocation or a new permission owner.",
2026-11-03T15:17:39.8587970Z   "live_custody_contract": "OCRM-CHANNEL-FAILURE-LIVE-CUSTODY-v1",
